<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eisenerz</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eisenerz is a mining town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/styria">Styria</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>, at the foot of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erzberg">Erzberg</a>, the 'iron ore mountain'. Iron ore has been mined there since the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>, and the town grew rich supplying the iron trade of Styria and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-austria">Upper Austria</a>. Its population has fallen sharply since the mine was mechanised in the 20th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eisenerz.jpg" alt="Eisenerz" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: C.Stadler/Bwag · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eisenerz_(5).JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
